Subject: RenderEngine: do not end SurfaceFlinger when a buffer cannot be wrapped as a texture

GaneshBackendTexture aborted with "Failed to create a valid texture" whenever Skia could not wrap
an AHardwareBuffer and the GPU device was not reported lost. On the owner's PC the window manager
(and with it the graphics renderer) restarted while an app was running: the app's next buffer
(848x1522) named a ColorBuffer the new renderer never made, the import failed, SurfaceFlinger
aborted in RenderEngine, and Android's user space restarted with every app. A buffer the GPU side
does not know is that buffer's problem: the texture stays invalid, makeImage and makeSurface give
nothing, the layer draws nothing from it, and the app's next buffer is imported on its own. A
buffer that says it has no size stays fatal, as it is a programming error.

Applies after the earlier patches for Android 16.
---
diff --git a/libs/renderengine/skia/compat/GaneshBackendTexture.cpp b/libs/renderengine/skia/compat/GaneshBackendTexture.cpp
index 77e5be7..1996eff 100644
--- a/libs/renderengine/skia/compat/GaneshBackendTexture.cpp
+++ b/libs/renderengine/skia/compat/GaneshBackendTexture.cpp
@@ -96,6 +96,16 @@ GaneshBackendTexture::GaneshBackendTexture(sk_sp<GrDirectContext> grContext,
         // buffer again on its new context.
         ALOGW("Failed to create a texture for a %dx%d buffer: the GPU device is lost", desc.width,
               desc.height);
+    } else if (!mBackendTexture.isValid() && desc.width && desc.height) {
+        // The context cannot wrap the buffer although the device is not lost. The buffer's
+        // memory is not known to the GPU side: an app that outlived a renderer restart still
+        // hands over buffers the new renderer never made, and a stream that ended fails every
+        // import. That is no programming error and must not end SurfaceFlinger, which would
+        // end every app: the texture stays invalid, the layer draws nothing from it, and the
+        // app's next buffer is imported on its own.
+        ALOGW("Failed to create a valid texture. [%p]:[%d,%d] isProtected:%d isWriteable:%d "
+              "format:%d; the layer shows nothing until its next buffer",
+              this, desc.width, desc.height, createProtectedImage, isOutputBuffer, desc.format);
     } else if (!mBackendTexture.isValid() || !desc.width || !desc.height) {
         LOG_ALWAYS_FATAL("Failed to create a valid texture. [%p]:[%d,%d] isProtected:%d "
                          "isWriteable:%d format:%d",
@@ -114,9 +124,11 @@ GaneshBackendTexture::~GaneshBackendTexture() {
 sk_sp<SkImage> GaneshBackendTexture::makeImage(SkAlphaType alphaType, ui::Dataspace dataspace,
                                                TextureReleaseProc releaseImageProc,
                                                ReleaseContext releaseContext) {
-    if (mBackendTexture.isValid()) {
-        mUpdateProc(mImageCtx, mGrContext.get());
+    if (!mBackendTexture.isValid()) {
+        // The buffer could not be wrapped (see the constructor); there is nothing to draw.
+        return nullptr;
     }
+    mUpdateProc(mImageCtx, mGrContext.get());
 
     const SkColorType colorType = colorTypeForImage(alphaType);
     sk_sp<SkImage> image =
@@ -136,6 +148,9 @@ sk_sp<SkImage> GaneshBackendTexture::makeImage(SkAlphaType alphaType, ui::Datasp
 sk_sp<SkSurface> GaneshBackendTexture::makeSurface(ui::Dataspace dataspace,
                                                    TextureReleaseProc releaseSurfaceProc,
                                                    ReleaseContext releaseContext) {
+    if (!mBackendTexture.isValid()) {
+        return nullptr;
+    }
     const SkColorType colorType = internalColorType();
     sk_sp<SkSurface> surface =
             SkSurfaces::WrapBackendTexture(mGrContext.get(), mBackendTexture,
